## ⚙️ Installation & Setup

### Prerequisites

Make sure the following software is installed:

* Node.js (v18 or above)
* PostgreSQL
* Git

---

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/avirajj93-commits/Project-Management.git
cd Project-Management
```

---

### 2️⃣ Setup Frontend

```bash
cd client
npm install
npm run dev
```

---

### 3️⃣ Setup Backend

```bash
cd server
npm install
```

---

### 4️⃣ Configure Environment Variables

Create `.env` files in both the `client` and `server` directories.

```env
DATABASE_URL=

CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
```

---

### 5️⃣ Run Database Migration

```bash
npx prisma db push
```

---

### 6️⃣ Start Backend Server

```bash
npm start
```

---

### 7️⃣ Access the Application

#### Frontend

```bash
http://localhost:5173
```

#### Backend

```bash
http://localhost:3000
```

